**3. Secret Management (Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, K8s Secrets)**
- **Secret Lifecycle:**
  - Storage: Encrypted at rest (AES-256-GCM)
  - Access: Least privilege (service-specific secrets)
  - Rotation: 90 days for service accounts, immediate on compromise
  - Audit: All secret access logged (who, what, when)
  
- **Detection & Prevention:**
  ```bash
  # Scan for secrets in code (pre-commit hook)
  truffleHog --regex --entropy git diff HEAD
  
  # Scan git history for historical secrets
  truffleHog --regex --entropy filesystem .
  
  # Validate secrets are in vault, not code
  grep -r "password\|secret\|api_key" src/ --exclude-dir=node_modules
  ```
  
- **Auto-Remediation:**
  - If secret detected in PR: Block merge, create incident ticket
  - If secret in git history: Force rotation, notify security team
  - Enforce: All secrets via environment variables or secret manager
  
**4. API Security Testing (Automated)**
- **Authentication Bypass:**
  ```bash
  # Test: Access protected endpoint without token
  curl https://api.example.com/api/v1/users/me
  # Expected: 401 Unauthorized
  
  # Test: Access with expired token
  curl -H "Authorization: Bearer <expired_token>" https://api.example.com/api/v1/users/me
  # Expected: 401 Unauthorized (not 500)
  ```
  
- **Authorization Bypass:**
  ```bash
  # Test: User A tries to access User B's data
  curl -H "Authorization: Bearer <userA_token>" https://api.example.com/api/v1/users/userB_id
  # Expected: 403 Forbidden
  
  # Test: Regular user tries admin endpoint
  curl -H "Authorization: Bearer <user_token>" https://api.example.com/api/v1/admin/users
  # Expected: 403 Forbidden
  ```
  
- **Injection Attacks:**
  ```bash
  # SQL Injection
  curl "https://api.example.com/api/v1/users?id=1' OR '1'='1"
  # Expected: 400 Bad Request or parameterized query prevents injection
  
  # NoSQL Injection
  curl -X POST https://api.example.com/api/v1/login \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"username": {"$ne": null}, "password": {"$ne": null}}'
  # Expected: 400 Bad Request or input validation blocks
  ```
  
- **Rate Limiting:**
  ```bash
  # Test: Burst 1000 requests in 1 second
  for i in {1..1000}; do
    curl https://api.example.com/api/v1/data &
  done
  # Expected: 429 Too Many Requests after threshold (100/min)
  ```

