# Security Configuration Standards

## Authentication
- Password policy: 12+ chars, complexity, breach checking (HaveIBeenPwned)
- MFA: TOTP minimum, WebAuthn/FIDO2 preferred
- Session: 15min idle timeout, 8hr absolute, secure + httpOnly + SameSite=strict
- JWT: RS256, 15min access, 7day refresh with rotation

## Authorization
- RBAC: Admin, Manager, User, Guest (default deny)
- Permission checks: Every endpoint, every action
- Ownership validation: User can only access own data (unless admin)

## Input Validation
- Whitelist approach: Known good, reject rest
- Output encoding: Context-appropriate (HTML, JS, URL, CSS)
- File uploads: Type validation, size limits, sandbox storage, virus scan

## Infrastructure
- HTTPS only: HSTS preload, 1 year max-age
- CSP: Strict policy, nonce-based, report-uri
- CORS: Whitelist only, no wildcards in production
- Security headers: X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy

## Secrets Management
- Never in code: Environment or vault only
- Rotation: 90 days for service accounts, immediate on compromise
- Least privilege: Each service own credentials, no shared accounts

